  "note": "An attack by infiltration (IBB S45 pp 221-230; DW s12 para 19 p 48, the desert best suited for it). The Bn moves from an assembly area close to the infiltration points, occupied a night before (IBB para 12 b p 224), through two lanes in the En FDL, two Coys and a Mor section in each half (para 14 a p 225), the shoulders of the gaps secured by the leading troops till the last man is through (para 23 p 228), to an RV and a firm base near the Obj beyond the En FDL: away from likely DF, protected, with alternative routes to the FUP and an alternative firm base (para 21 p 227; DW p 48 a: an RV / firm base in the vicinity of the Obj with multiple routes leading to it, avoiding the En posns). From the firm base the assault goes in as a normal attack. By night (DW p 48), within the Div artillery's range (IBB para 7 p 222; medium guns, DW p 48 c), an alternative Obj given (para 5 p 222), link-up within 24-36 h with the administrative cover for it (para 10 p 223), the Obj seized and held till then (DW p 48 d). Lanes through the En minefields cleared on the preceding nights, 2-3 nights (para 25 p 228). The distances here are a decision (E): the En FDL 4 km short of the FUP, the RV 1.3 km and the firm base 0.9 km short of it.",
